    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "j2lsX",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1310,
      "name": "BRIEF — Studio · mobile 2",
      "clip": true,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 1180,
      "fill": "$paper",
      "cornerRadius": "$radius-2xl",
      "stroke": "$line",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 10,
      "padding": 32,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "I9FXAk",
          "name": "Heading",
          "fill": "$graphite",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "BRIEF — Studio · mobile 2",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "NWevI",
          "name": "Body",
          "fill": "$graphite",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "kit-version-source: 0.1.0 · brief-schema: 1 · updated: 2026-09-27\nTHE DESIGN WE WANT, compared against the app. In code (#110, #112, #113): the piece in the panel, one status chip, notices resolved together, Field and readable text. Pending: amber for selection only (K6), the expert's memory next to the conversation (UI-4). Screens named \"capture\" are the app as it is and stay that way.\n1. PURPOSE\nThe rest of the Studio's sections in the same grammar as band 1.\n2. ENTRY POINTS\nTap a piece, \"Editar a mano\"; the Mueble and Materiales tabs; the version button in the header.\n3. SCREENS (columns are areas; a column's states stack below it)\n- Piece / Editing by hand — the edit form lives in the piece sheet, the 3D stays whole (B-2); move buttons follow the piece's axis (PieceEditor.tsx MOVE)\n- Furniture / Plan sheet — the tab is the plan sheet only; the kind is one compact line; the expert's memory moves next to the conversation (UI-4, not drawn yet)\n- Materials / Fix before buying — cost first (UI-16), then the verdict and the checks; sentence-case labels (UI-2)\n- Notices / Nothing pending, Furniture / No plan sheet, Materials / Sheets to buy and Sheet layout: captures of the app, unchanged\n- History / Two versions — a flat timeline, no card inside a card; \"Volver a esta\" is a visible button (UI-17 family)\n- Captures of the app for the states that stay as they are: the expert asks with options, the expert failed with \"Reintentar\", a hand edit rejected with its alternatives, the plan sheet with changes, a kind change that needs a redo, reviewing, not viable with \"Ver la lista de todos modos\", cut settings, editing a price, viewing an old version, the expert's settings, unlocking saved keys, and confirming \"Nuevo diseño\"\n- PROPOSAL (UI-4, not approved): Conversation / Expert's memory, open — the memory leaves the Furniture tab and folds above the conversation; closed it is one line with a count\nK6 ON THE CAPTURES: amber that is not selection or focus turns neutral when K6 lands — the kind-redo box, the materials price note, the SheLLM box and the lock icon on unlock\nKNOWN BUG: on unlock at 390 px \"Desbloquear\" overflows its card (the Input needs min-w-0; K7 regression, B-3)\n4. BUSINESS RULES\nHand edits apply at once and are checked like any change; the plan applies on \"Aplicar\" (D34). The list stays behind the review (D30).\n5. COPY SOURCE\nsrc/ui/studio/{PieceEditor,FurniturePanel,PlanSheet,Materials,Verdict,HistoryPanel}.tsx; verdict text from the simulated expert. \"~$3,165\" from the v2 capture.\n6. STATES NOT DRAWN\nNone.\n7. OPEN FINDINGS\nUI-2, UI-4, UI-16, UI-17, B-2\n8. HISTORY\n→ LOG frame, below.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
