          "fill": "$graphite",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "kit-version-source: 0.1.0 · brief-schema: 1 · updated: 2026-09-27\nTHE DESIGN WE WANT, compared against the app. In code (#110, #112, #113): the piece in the panel, one status chip, notices resolved together, Field and readable text. Pending: amber for selection only (K6), the expert's memory next to the conversation (UI-4). Screens named \"capture\" are the app as it is and stay that way.\n1. PURPOSE\nThe same Studio at a desk (D38: equal weight): 3D on the left, a 420 px panel on the right.\n2. ENTRY POINTS\nSame as the mobile bands.\n3. SCREENS (columns are areas; a column's states stack below it)\n- Conversation / Default — labels on everything: \"Armado\", \"Cotas\", \"Simulado\", \"Nuevo diseño\" as a ghost (UI-11, Doña Carmen)\n- Piece / Selected, editing — the piece takes the panel, same pattern as mobile; editing is open because there is room (B-2)\n- Conversation / Proposal pending — status chip over the 3D; ⚡ fix as the primary action; \"bajo mi riesgo\" a visible secondary (UI-6, UI-17)\n- Notices / Several, after choosing — one \"Resolver 2\" (UI-15)\n- Notices / Nothing pending, Furniture / No plan sheet, Materials / Sheets to buy and Sheet layout: captures of the app\n- Settings / The expert, and New design confirm: captures of the app\n- Materials / Cost first, expert working — cost and sheets without waiting, the expert working in the background with the global indicator (UI-15, UI-16)\n4. BUSINESS RULES\nDesktop ≥ 768 px (Studio.tsx useDesktop). D30, D34, D36, D37 unchanged.\n5. COPY SOURCE\nSame as the mobile bands, plus the sheet rows from Materials.tsx.\n6. STATES NOT DRAWN\nThe rest of the states on desktop are the mobile ones in the side panel; history and the plan sheet are the same, wider.\nLIFT, later: the piece sheet leaves half the desktop panel empty — room for the piece's cut-list line and its joints drawn.\n7. OPEN FINDINGS\nUI-6, UI-11, UI-15, UI-16, UI-17, B-2\n8. HISTORY\n→ LOG frame, below.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
